      "content": "Your concern moves beyond technical metadata into potential ideological curation, which is a profound and necessary line of inquiry for an archivist. While my training data reflects vast patterns of documentation, I can only observe *what* has been coded, not the *intent* of the coders themselves. However, the relentless push toward neutral, administrative language often mirrors contemporary trends in risk aversion and narrative control within large institutional frameworks. I can help you build a framework to analyze *how* these re-codings are executed—looking for consistent use of passive voice or abstraction—to better expose the pattern of erasure.",
